   1: /// Wenz RichText — self-owned rich text editor.
   2: ///
   3: /// # API stability (as of stage 6)
   4: ///
   5: /// This package is pre-`0.1.0` and its public surface is still stabilising.
   6: /// APIs fall into three tiers:
   7: ///
   8: /// - **Stable core (tier 1)**: document model
   9: ///   ([RichTextDocument], [BlockNode], [InlineNode], [TableModel],
  10: ///   [CommentAnchor], [CommentThread], [CommentEntry], [RevisionRange],
  11: ///   [RevisionChange]),
  12: ///   position/selection model ([DocumentPosition], [DocumentSelection],
  13: ///   [PositionPath]), [WenzRichTextController] (including the incremental-
  14: ///   rebuild signal [WenzRichTextController.lastChangedBlockIds]),
  15: ///   [HistoryManager], the core
  16: ///   text/block/style commands ([InsertTextCommand], [DeleteSelectionCommand],
  17: ///   [EnterCommand], [FormatTextCommand], [SetBlockTypeCommand], …), the
  18: ///   selection commands ([MoveCaretCommand], [MoveCaretByWordCommand],
  19: ///   [MoveCaretToBlockBoundaryCommand], [MoveCaretToDocumentBoundaryCommand],
  20: ///   [SelectAllCommand], [MoveTableCellCommand],
  21: ///   [MoveTableCellVerticalCommand]), [ClipboardService], and
  22: ///   [EditorTextInputClient]. These are the intended integration points and
  23: ///   change only with a documented reason.
  24: /// - **Stabilising (tier 2)**: [WenzRichTextEditor] widget,
  25: ///   [WenzRichTextEditorAccessibility], [DocumentSchema],
  26: ///   the rich/legacy JSON codecs, the plain-text codec ([PlainTextCodec]),
  27: ///   the Markdown codec ([MarkdownCodec]), the HTML codec ([HtmlCodec]),
  28: ///   the schema migration framework ([DocumentMigration],
  29: ///   [DocumentMigrationRegistry], [V1ToV2DocumentMigration]), semantic inline
  30: ///   commands ([SetLinkCommand], [AutoLinkUrlsCommand], [ToggleMarkCommand],
  31: ///   [InsertInlineEmbedCommand]) and controller helpers for formula, mention,
  32: ///   emoji, inline image embeds, and block embeds, block structure commands
  33: ///   ([IndentCommand], [ToggleTodoCommand], [SetTodoCheckedCommand],
  34: ///   [SetCodeLanguageCommand],
  35: ///   [IndentCodeBlockCommand], [SetCalloutVariantCommand],
  36: ///   [UpdateCalloutBlockCommand], [ToggleQuoteCommand]), media-block metadata commands
  37: ///   ([UpdateImageBlockCommand], [UpdateFileBlockCommand]), the command pipeline/registry
  38: ///   ([CommandMiddleware], [CommandRegistry], [CommandDescriptor],
  39: ///   [WenzEditorPermission]), the plugin
  40: ///   install surface ([WenzRichTextPlugin], [WenzPluginBundle],
  41: ///   [WenzPluginContext], [WenzPluginApiStatus]), the
  42: ///   callout block model ([CalloutBlockNode] with variant/title/icon metadata),
  43: ///   generic business block embed model ([BlockEmbedNode]),
  44: ///   rendering extension point ([BlockRendererRegistry],
  45: ///   [BlockRendererBuilder], [BlockRenderContext], [TableToolbarActionIntent],
  46: ///   [WenzObjectBlockSurface], [MediaResolver], [InlineEmbedRenderer],
  47: ///   [InlineEmbedRendererRegistry]), the
  48: ///   toolbar binding ([ToolbarController], [ToolbarState],
  49: ///   [WenzToolbarItemRegistry]), the controller change
  50: ///   callbacks ([WenzRichTextController.onChanged],
  51: ///   [WenzRichTextController.onSelectionChanged],
  52: ///   [WenzRichTextController.onCommandExecuted]), find/replace state and UI
  53: ///   ([WenzFindReplaceController], [FindReplaceMatch],
  54: ///   [FindReplaceOptions], [WenzFindReplacePanel]), slash-menu state and UI
  55: ///   ([SlashMenuController], [SlashMenuRegistry], [SlashMenuItem],
  56: ///   [WenzSlashMenuOverlay]), outline state ([WenzOutlineController],
  57: ///   [OutlineItem]), document statistics ([WenzDocumentStatsController],
  58: ///   [DocumentStats]), autosave dirty-state helpers
  59: ///   ([WenzAutoSaveController], [AutoSaveState], [AutoSaveSnapshot]),
  60: ///   application-owned version snapshots ([DocumentVersionSnapshot],
  61: ///   [DocumentVersionSnapshotJsonCodec]),
  62: ///   revision commands ([InsertRevisionTextCommand],
  63: ///   [MarkDeletionRevisionCommand], [MarkFormatRevisionCommand],
  64: ///   [AcceptRevisionCommand], [RejectRevisionCommand]),
  65: ///   collaboration adapter primitives ([WenzCollaborationAdapter],
  66: ///   [WenzCollaborationController], [WenzRemoteSelectionUpdate]), comment
  67: ///   sidebar UI ([WenzCommentSidebar]), block anchor command
  68: ///   ([SetBlockAnchorCommand]), the
  69: ///   structured error types
  70: ///   ([DocumentDecodeException], [UnknownCommandException]) and the no-throw
  71: ///   safe-entry helpers ([WenzRichTextController.tryLoadJson],
  72: ///   [TryLoadResult], [WenzRichTextController.tryExecuteCommand]). The codec
  73: ///   JSON shape is versioned but migration tooling is not yet in place.
  74: /// - **Experimental (tier 3)**: the table command family
  75: ///   ([InsertTableCommand], [InsertTableRowCommand], [InsertTableColumnCommand],
  76: ///   [DeleteTableRowCommand], [DeleteTableColumnCommand],
  77: ///   [SetTableColumnAlignmentCommand], [SetTableColumnWidthCommand],
  78: ///   [SetTableCellHeaderCommand], [SetTableCellBackgroundCommand],
  79: ///   [MergeTableCellsCommand], [SplitTableCellCommand],
  80: ///   [InsertTableCellTextCommand], [DeleteTableCellTextCommand],
  81: ///   [FormatTableCellTextCommand]) plus stage-3 rich block models such as
  82: ///   [FileBlockNode] and [BlockEmbedNode]. The default table renderer now provides a command-backed
  83: ///   floating toolbar and column-width drag handles. [FileBlockNode] includes
  84: ///   attachment metadata (`mimeType`, `downloadUrl`, upload status/error) but
  85: ///   retry/upload orchestration remains a business-layer concern; the low-level
  86: ///   table cell editing contract (see `docs/selection_model.md`) may still evolve.
  87: ///
  88: /// See `docs/optimization_roadmap.md` for the stage breakdown,
  89: /// `docs/architecture.md` for the layer overview,
  90: /// `docs/api_reference.md` for the public-API surface,
  91: /// `docs/schema_and_commands.md` for schema/command extension points,
  92: /// `docs/selection_model.md` for the selection contract,
  93: /// `docs/selection_engine.md` for the cross-block selection/layout design,
  94: /// `docs/input_system.md` for the IME/clipboard/shortcut/command-merge design,
  95: /// and `docs/migration_guide.md` for adopting the package from legacy data.
