   5: /// Resolves a media block ([ImageBlockNode], [VideoBlockNode], or
   6: /// [FileBlockNode]) into a display widget.
   7: ///
   8: /// Inject an instance via `WenzRichTextEditor.mediaResolver` (and, for
   9: /// convenience, `WenzRichTextController.mediaResolver`) to take over how media
  10: /// blocks render. The default image/video/file renderers first ask the
  11: /// resolver; when it returns `null` (or when no resolver is injected) they fall
  12: /// back to built-in rendering (image/video placeholders, file metadata card).
  13: ///
  14: /// Returning a widget (rather than an `ImageProvider`/URL) keeps the resolver
  15: /// fully general: the business layer assembles its own `Image`, a video
  16: /// player, a download chip, or any custom widget, using whatever source it
  17: /// owns (network, local file, memory bytes, signed URL, …). The package never
  18: /// needs to depend on `video_player`/`image`/etc. — that stays a business
  19: /// concern.
  20: ///
  21: /// ```dart
  22: /// class NetworkImageResolver implements MediaResolver {
  23: ///   @override
  24: ///   Widget? resolve(BuildContext context, BlockNode block) {
  25: ///     if (block is! ImageBlockNode) return null;
  26: ///     final url = block.file.isNotEmpty ? block.file : block.assetId;
