  29: ///       url,
  30: ///       fit: BoxFit.contain,
  31: ///       errorBuilder: (_, __, ___) => const Text('image load failed'),
  32: ///     );
  33: ///   }
  34: /// }
  35: /// ```
  36: ///
  37: /// Throwing from [resolve] is tolerated: the editor catches it and falls back
  38: /// to the placeholder, so a faulty resolver never crashes the editor (see
  39: /// `docs/schema_and_commands.md` §Error handling).
  40: abstract class MediaResolver {
  41:   /// Builds the widget for [block], or `null` to let the editor fall back to
  42:   /// its built-in placeholder for that block.
  43:   ///
  44:   /// [context] is the build context the block is being painted in (use it for
  45:   /// `MediaQuery`/`Theme`/`DefaultTextStyle`). The block is guaranteed to be
  46:   /// an [ImageBlockNode], [VideoBlockNode], or [FileBlockNode] — the only
  47:   /// block types whose default renderers consult a resolver.
