  80: );
  81: ```
  82: 
  83: Resolution order for `BlockEmbedNode`: an exact `registerEmbed(embedType, ...)`
  84: builder wins; otherwise the generic `BlockType.embed` renderer paints the built-
  85: in placeholder. Rich JSON and HTML round-trip the structured embed fields;
  86: Markdown/plain text intentionally degrade to readable fallback text.
  87: 
  88: ## Default renderers
  89: 
  90: `WenzRichTextEditor.installDefaultRenderers` registers one builder per
  91: `BlockType`:
  92: 
  93: | BlockType | Renderer | Notes |
  94: | --- | --- | --- |
  95: | paragraph / heading / quote / listItem | `_TextBlockRenderer` | Inline-aware; formula/mention fallback + optional `InlineEmbedRenderer`; selection/caret/composition via `_TextSelectionSurface`. |
  96: | code | `_CodeBlockRenderer` | Monospace body with composition underline span; toolbar includes language dropdown and copy-code button. Language changes call `SetCodeLanguageCommand`; Tab/Shift+Tab in the editor call `IndentCodeBlockCommand`. |
  97: | image / video / file | asks `MediaResolver`, then built-in fallback | Built-in media renderers consult the injected [MediaResolver] first; when it returns `null` (or no resolver is set) images/videos fall back to `_MediaPlaceholder`, while files fall back to a metadata card. Image blocks wrap the result with `showWidth`/`showHeight` sizing and optional caption text; file cards show display name, size, MIME type, upload status, and failure text. See [Media resolver](#media-resolver). |
  98: | embed | `_BlockEmbedContent` or business renderer | Generic block embed placeholder displays `embedType` + `fallbackText`/data label. Register per business type with `BlockRendererRegistry.registerEmbed`; wrap large custom widgets in `WenzObjectBlockSurface` for object-block selection semantics. |
  99: | table | `_TableBlockRenderer` | Custom Stack grid layout; visible cells are positioned by `rowSpan`/`columnSpan`, covered cells are not rendered or hit-tested; table-cell text uses the same inline embed fallback/renderer path. When a table cell/range is selected, the default renderer shows a floating toolbar for row/column insert/delete, header/background/alignment, merge/split, width reset, plus drag handles that persist explicit column widths via `SetTableColumnWidthCommand`. |
 100: | divider | Flutter `Divider`. | |
 101: | callout | `_CalloutRenderer` | Variant-tinted surface with icon, title, body, and an editable type dropdown for `info`/`success`/`warning`/`danger`; uses the same inline embed fallback/renderer path. |
 102: 
 103: ## Inline embed renderer
 104: 
 105: `InlineEmbedRenderer` (`lib/src/widgets/inline_embed_renderer.dart`) is the
 106: quick path for formula / mention / emoji / custom inline embed text rendering without
 107: replacing the whole paragraph renderer:
 108: 
 109: ```dart
 110: final renderer = InlineEmbedRendererCallback((context, embed, style) {
 111:   if (embed.embedType == 'formula') {
 112:     return TextSpan(text: "formula(${embed.data['text']})", style: style);
 113:   }
 114:   return null; // keep the built-in fallback for mention / emoji / image / custom types.
 115: });
 116: 
 117: WenzRichTextEditor(
 118:   controller: controller,
 119:   inlineEmbedRenderer: renderer,
 120: );
 121: ```
 122: 
 123: The editor still treats every `InlineEmbed` as one logical character for caret
 124: movement and selection. Prefer compact `TextSpan`s here; use
 125: `BlockRendererRegistry` when a feature needs a large interactive widget.
 126: Built-in fallbacks display formula text, mention `@label`, emoji unicode, inline
 127: images as `[img]`, and unknown custom types as `[type]`.
 128: 
 129: ## Media resolver
 130: 
 131: `MediaResolver` (`lib/src/widgets/media_resolver.dart`) is the quick path for
 132: real image/video/file rendering without replacing an entire block renderer:
 133: 
 134: ```dart
 135: class NetworkImageResolver implements MediaResolver {
 136:   @override
 137:   Widget? resolve(BuildContext context, BlockNode block) {
 138:     if (block is! ImageBlockNode) return null;
 139:     final url = block.file.isNotEmpty ? block.file : block.assetId;
 140:     if (!url.startsWith('http')) return null;       // let the placeholder show
 141:     return Image.network(url, fit: BoxFit.contain,
 142:       errorBuilder: (_, e, __) => const Text('image load failed'));
 143:   }
 144: }
 145: 
 146: final resolver = NetworkImageResolver();
 147: final controller = WenzRichTextController(document: doc, mediaResolver: resolver);
 148: 
 149: WenzRichTextEditor(controller: controller, mediaResolver: resolver);
 150: ```
 151: 
 152: Inject the resolver in **two places**: the editor widget (drives rendering) and
 153: the controller (business-layer handle, e.g. for an upload helper). The same
 154: instance should be shared.
 155: 
 156: Semantics:
 157: 
 158: - Returning a widget (rather than an `ImageProvider`/URL) keeps the resolver
 159:   fully general — the business layer assembles `Image`, a video player, a
 160:   download chip, or any custom widget, using whatever source it owns. The
 161:   package never needs to depend on `video_player`/`image`/etc.
 162: - Returning `null` declines the block → the editor falls back to the built-in
 163:   placeholder. Use this to handle only some media types or some sources.
 164: - Throwing from `resolve` is tolerated: the editor catches it, reports the
 165:   error via `FlutterError.reportError` (so it surfaces in dev tools), and falls
 166:   back to the placeholder. A faulty resolver never crashes the editor.
 167: - Upload is a business concern: create or insert a `FileBlockNode` with
 168:   `uploadStatus: FileUploadStatus.pending/uploading`, then store the resulting
 169:   URL in `downloadUrl` (or legacy `file`) and flip status to `uploaded` via
 170:   `WenzRichTextController.updateFileBlock`. On failure, set
 171:   `uploadStatus: FileUploadStatus.failed` and `uploadError`; business UI or a
 172:   custom `MediaResolver` can expose a retry button and drive another update.
 173: - Image metadata stays on `ImageBlockNode`: use
 174:   `WenzRichTextController.updateImageBlock` to update natural size
 175:   (`width`/`height`), display size (`showWidth`/`showHeight`), `caption`, and
 176:   `altText`. The default image renderer shows the caption below either the
 177:   resolver widget or fallback placeholder; semantics prefer `altText`, then
 178:   caption, then the asset/file label.
 179: 
 180: ### MediaResolver vs BlockRendererRegistry
 181: 
 182: Both are extension points for block rendering; pick by scope:
 183: 
 184: - **`MediaResolver`** — narrow, media-only. The built-in image/video/file
 185:   renderers consult it. Lowest effort; ideal when you just want real media
 186:   decoding.
 187: - **`BlockRendererRegistry`** — whole-block replacement for any `BlockType`,
 188:   including media, plus per-`BlockEmbedNode.embedType` business renderers. Use
 189:   it when you need to change the surrounding chrome (selection/caret
 190:   participation, custom layout), override a non-media block, or render a custom
 191:   business block embed.
 192: 
 193: Priority for a media block: a custom `BlockRendererRegistry` entry wins (it
 194: replaces the whole renderer, which would not consult the resolver at all);
 195: otherwise the default renderer asks the `MediaResolver`; otherwise the
 196: placeholder.
 197: 
 198: ## Virtualisation (large documents)
 199: 
 200: Blocks are laid out lazily via `ListView.separated`: only blocks inside the
 201: viewport (plus a small overflow buffer the sliver keeps) are built. Each block
 202: is wrapped in `_KeepAliveBlock`, a `StatefulWidget` mixing in
 203: `AutomaticKeepAliveClientMixin`. The editor marks the **caret block** (collapsed
 204: selection) and the **selection endpoints** (`base` / `extent` block ids) as
 205: keep-alive, so they stay mounted even after they scroll out of view.
 206: 
 207: Why keep-alive matters: selection highlight, the caret, and click hit-testing
 208: are all painted/resolved *inside* each mounted `_TextSelectionSurface` (and
 209: registered with the `BlockGeometryRegistry` on mount). Keeping the caret and
 210: selection endpoints mounted guarantees:
